update public.moo_versions set body_md = body_md || E'<th><p>In: Register; LOG-F03</p>\n<p>Out: Updated PTN-F01 and LOG-F03</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: During the forum</p>\n<p>Control: Changes dated</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Learn</th>\n<th>Facilitator</th>\n<th><p>Review what worked with partners last season and agree improvements.</p>\n<p>Decision: Improvements agreed?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: AAR findings</p>\n<p>Out: Forum record; ME-F08 entries</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: During the forum</p>\n<p>Control: Lessons logged (Chapter 7)</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Follow up</th>\n<th>Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Send the forum record; enter actions in the CAPA register.</p>\n<p>Decision: Actions owned?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Forum record</p>\n<p>Out: ME-F05 entries</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 15 days</p>\n<p>Control: Tracked to closure</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMC</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Forum pack; invitations and attendance; updated register and inventory; forum record; lessons and CAPA entries.\n\n### SOP 8-08 \\| Assistance to Other LGUs\n**Process owner:** CDRRMO Head as CDRRMC secretariat. **Purpose:** Give help to other LGUs through a lawful, documented route that does not weaken the City''s own readiness.\n\n**Table 8.24**\n\n**SOP 8-08 Control Block**\n\n| **Control Element**         | **Entry**                                                                                                         |\n|-----------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Type and MODE template      | Workflow: WF-SOP8-08 (proposed)                                                                                   |\n| Decision authority (legal)  | CDRRMC recommends; SP authorises; City Mayor approves; funds and procurement under Chapter 6                      |\n| Process owner (operational) | CDRRMO Head                                                                                                       |\n| Trigger                     | A request from, or a disaster in, another LGU                                                                     |\n| Forms                       | PTN-F03 (outbound); FIN forms as Chapter 6 requires                                                               |\n| IAT v1.7 indicators         | A10.1 (1, Medium)                                                                                                 |\n| Functional MR links         | MR-02                                                                                                             |\n| Policy basis                | RA 7160 Sec. 33; RA 10121; JMC 2013-1 and the applicable proclamation or rule on use of the LDRRMF for other LGUs |\n| Cross-references            | Chapter 6 (SOPs 6-02, 6-04); SOP 8-02                                                                             |\n\n**Table 8.25**\n\n**SOP 8-08 Steps and Controls**\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 12%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 29%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and Decision Rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and Outputs / Records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, Control and Escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>1. Assess</th>\n<th>CDRRMO Head</th>\n<th><p>Assess the request and the City''s own risk: is any hazard threatening Ormoc in the same period?</p>\n<p>Decision: City readiness kept?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Request; forecasts</p>\n<p>Out: Assessment note</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 24 hours</p>\n<p>Control: Own stocks not drawn below Chapter 6 levels without a decision</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMC Chair</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>2. Confirm the legal basis</th>\n<th>City Legal Office; City Budget Officer</th>\n<th><p>Confirm the fund source and its legal basis (for example, a mutual aid agreement or a proclamation allowing LDRRMF use for other LGUs).</p>\n<p>Decision: Lawful source identified?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Assessment note</p>\n<p>Out: Legal and budget advice</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 48 hours</p>\n<p>Control: Basis cited in the resolution</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Administrator</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>3. Recommend and authorise</th>\n<th>CDRRMC; SP</th>\n<th><p>Recommend by CDRRMC resolution; SP authorises.</p>\n<p>Decision: Authorised?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Advice</p>\n<p>Out: Resolutions</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Special session if needed</p>\n<p>Control: Resolution numbers recorded</p>\n<p>Escalate: City Mayor</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="header">\n<th>4. Deliver</th>\n<th>Administration and Training; CSWDO; Treasurer</th>\n<th><p>Deliver cash, goods or teams; obtain receipts.</p>\n<p>Decision: Receipt obtained?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Resolutions</p>\n<p>Out: Transfer and receipt records</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Per agreement</p>\n<p>Control: COA rules followed (Chapter 6)</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<th>5. Record</th>\n<th>Administration and Training</th>\n<th><p>Record the assistance in the partner register and the quarterly report.</p>\n<p>Decision: Recorded?</p></th>\n<th><p>In: Receipts</p>\n<p>Out: PTN-F01 entry; FIN-F03 entry</p></th>\n<th><p>Time: Within 15 days</p>\n<p>Control: Disclosed with the quarterly report</p>\n<p>Escalate: CDRRMO Head</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Minimum records:** Assessment note; legal and budget advice; resolutions; transfer and receipt records; register and report entries.\n\n## 15. Responsibility Assignment (RACI)\n\n| **\\[R\\] Responsible** | **\\[A\\] Accountable** | **\\[C\\] Consulted** | **\\[I\\] Informed** |\n|-----------------------|-----------------------|---------------------|--------------------|\n\n"A" is the single proposed process-accountable owner; "R" performs; "C" is consulted; "I" is informed. The RACI allocates work; it does not transfer legal powers.\n\n**Table 8.26**\n\n*RACI for Stakeholder Engagement and Partnerships*\n\n| **Activity**                            | **MY** | **SP** | **CC** | **HD** | **AT** | **RP** | **EOC** | **LG** | **LO** | **PT** | **CA** |\n|-----------------------------------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|---------|--------|--------|--------|--------|\n| Partner register and agreements         | A      | A      | C      | R      | R      | I      | I       | R      | C      | R      | I      |\n| Inter-LGU mutual aid agreement          | A      | A      | C      | R      | R      | C      | C       | R      | –      | R      | I      |\n| Mutual aid activation                   | A      | I      | I      | R      | C      | –      | R       | –      | –      | R      | I      |\n| Augmentation request and incoming teams | A      | I      | I      | R      | C      | C      | R       | –      | C      | R      | I      |\n| Part C interface agreements and review  | I      | –      | I      | R      | C      | R      | –       | C      | A      | –      | A      |\n| Utility restoration arrangements        | A      | A      | I      | R      | C      | C      | R       | C      | C      | R      | I      |\n| CDRRMC partner seats                    | A      | A      | C      | R      | R      | –      | –       | R      | –      | C      | I      |\n| Annual partner forum                    | I      | I      | A      | R      | R      | C      | C       | –      | C      | C      | I      |\n| Assistance to other LGUs                | A      | A      | C      | R      | R      | –      | –       | C      | C      | –      | I      |\n\n*Note. MY = City Mayor; SP = Sangguniang Panlungsod; CC = CDRRMC; HD = CDRRMO Head; AT = CDRRMO Administration and Training; RP = CDRRMO Research and Planning; EOC = EOC Manager and staff; LG = City Legal Office; LO = Part C lead offices; PT = partner organisation or LGU; CA = City Administrator. Where a row has two "A" entries, each holds a distinct act: the SP authorises and the Mayor signs; for Part C, each lead office is accountable for its own indicators and the City Administrator approves interface agreements; for the CDRRMC seats, the SP accredits CSOs and the Mayor issues the EO.*\n\n## 16. Performance Monitoring, Quality Assurance and Corrective Action\n\n**Table 8.27**\n\n*Performance Measures for Chapter 8*\n\n| **Measure**                                                                                  | **Evidence**                    | **Review Owner** |\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------|------------------|\n| Share of DRRM partnerships with a signed, authorised agreement in force                      | PTN-F01; Vault copies           | CDRRMC           |\n| Agreements reviewed in the last 12 months                                                    | PTN-F01 review dates            | CDRRMO Head      |\n| Mutual aid agreements in force with neighbouring LGUs                                        | Signed agreements               | CDRRMC           |\n| Part C lead offices with a signed interface agreement; Interface Index trend                 | PTN-F04; IAT Part C results     | CDRRMC           |\n| Utilities with a restoration-priority arrangement; restoration times for priority facilities | PTN-F06; EOC logs               | CDRRMO Head      |\n| CDRRMC partner seats filled by accredited, active members                                    | PTN-F07; attendance             | CDRRMC           |\n| Annual partner forum held before the season; actions closed                                  | Forum record; ME-F05            | CDRRMO Head      |\n| Augmentation requests acknowledged and fulfilled; time to arrival                            | PTN-F03; MODE resource requests | EOC Manager      |\n\nFindings go to the CAPA register under Chapter 7 (SOP 7-05).\n\n## 17. Implementation, Validation and Institutionalisation Priorities\n\n**Table 8.28**\n\n*Implementation Priorities for Chapter 8*\n\n| **No.** | **Action**                                                                                                                                                                         | **Office**                                                     | **IAT**      | **When**                       |\n|---------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|--------------|--------------------------------|\n| 1       | Open the partner register (PTN-F01) with all existing agreements; obtain the signed CPR-RIMT MOA; file signed copies of the NRC, OML Center and tertiary-institutions instruments. | Administration and Training                                    | A10.2        | Before the workshop            |\n| 2       | Agree with the Building Official the list of facilities for structural assessment and the rapid pre-impact inspection checklist.                                                   | City Engineer / Building Official; CDRRMO                      | C2.1 (High)  | First quarter 2027             |\n| 3       | Convene the CHO and hospitals on the health anticipatory action plan.                                                                                                              | CHO; hospitals; CDRRMO                                         | C4.1 (High)  | First quarter 2027             |\n| 4       | Propose technical mutual aid agreements to Kananga, Albuera, Merida, Isabel and the Province.                                                                                      | CDRRMO Head                                                    | A10.1        | First quarter 2027             |\n| 5       | Sign interface agreements (PTN-F04) with every Part C lead office; confirm focal persons in MODE.                                                                                  | CDRRMO Research and Planning; lead offices; City Administrator | MR-17        | Within 90 days of adoption     |\n| 6       | Agree restoration-priority arrangements with LEYECO V, NGCP, telecom providers and water services.                                                                                 | CDRRMO Head                                                    | C2.2         | Before the 2027 typhoon season |\n| 7       | Issue the amending EO: City College of Ormoc and an academe seat; third private-sector seat; SP accreditation of CSOs cited.                                                       | CDRRMO; City Legal Office; Mayor                               | A1.2         | First quarter 2027             |\n| 8       | Hold the first annual partner forum, inviting faith-based and sectoral groups.                                                                                                     | CDRRMO Head                                                    | A10.2        | April–May 2027                 |\n| 9       | Platform: add a partner agreements table (type, instrument, term, focal persons, review date) linked to offices and resources; load templates for SOPs 8-01 to 8-08.               | Platform data custodian                                        | MR-02, MR-08 | With the next release          |\n\nValidation: each SOP is reviewed by the offices named in its control block; the mutual aid and augmentation protocols are tested in a joint exercise with at least one neighbouring LGU; agreements are adopted only after City Legal Office review.\n\n## 18. Forms, Registers 