 6.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Write the declogging and debris protocol.                                                                                                        |\n| C4.1    | CHO; hospitals    | 3              | 1         | 9.0 High         | MR-05; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Prepare the health anticipatory action plan with the CHO and hospitals.                                                                          |\n| C4.2    | DepEd SDO         | 2              | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-05; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Obtain school AA plans and learning-continuity modalities; agree class suspension and school-use triggers.                                       |\n| C4.3    | Agri; Vet         | 2              | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-05; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Draft agri-fisheries early action guidelines using RSBSA and FishR; file the El Niño Task Force plan.                                            |\n| C4.4    | DTI; market       | 1              | 1         | 3.0 Low          | MR-05; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Agree pre-impact price monitoring with DTI Leyte and the market office.                                                                          |\n| C5.1    | CDRRMO; Chamber   | 1              | 1         | 3.0 Low          | MR-04; MR-17; MR-18                  | 8-04       | Run business continuity outreach with the Chamber using CDRA scenarios.                                                                          |\n\n*Note. Copied from IAT v1.7 and the Traceability and Data Dictionary v1.2. For Part C rows the master requirements shown are those specific to the row; every row also carries MR-01 and MR-12 to MR-15. Part C rows carry the lead office in the Type column and are scored into the Interface Index, not the IMI.*\n\n## Annex 8-B. Model Outline of a Technical Mutual Aid Agreement\n\n**Table 8.32**\n\n*Outline of a Technical Mutual Aid Agreement*\n\n| **No.** | **Article**                     | **Content to Be Negotiated**                                                                                   |\n|---------|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Parties and authority           | LGUs; sanggunian resolutions authorising each Mayor; optional accession by the Province                        |\n| 2       | Purpose and principles          | Technical cooperation in DRRM; reciprocity; no transfer of authority; each party first protects its own people |\n| 3       | Definitions                     | Requesting party, assisting party, resources, deployment, host Incident Commander                              |\n| 4       | Resources covered               | Types of teams, equipment and services; annexed lists updated yearly                                           |\n| 5       | Activation                      | Who may request; request content; response time; right to decline                                              |\n| 6       | Command, control and safety     | Under the host IC (ICS); own supervisors; right of recall                                                      |\n| 7       | Logistics                       | Self-sufficiency period; food, lodging and fuel arrangements                                                   |\n| 8       | Costs and settlement            | What each party bears; reimbursement method; timing                                                            |\n| 9       | Liability and insurance         | Personnel and equipment insurance; claims; indemnity                                                           |\n| 10      | Information and data            | Directory, warnings and SitRep exchange; data protection                                                       |\n| 11      | Exercises and review            | Annual joint exercise or call-down; annual review                                                              |\n| 12      | Term, amendment and termination | Duration; renewal; notice period                                                                               |\n\n## Annex 8-C. Model Outline of a Part C Interface Agreement\n\n**Table 8.33**\n\n*Outline of an Interface Agreement Between the CDRRMO and a Lead Office*\n\n| **No.** | **Section**           | **Content**                                                                                                        |\n|---------|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Parties and approval  | CDRRMO and the lead office; approved by the City Administrator (or included in a Mayor''s EO)                       |\n| 2       | Indicators owned      | Part C indicator codes and statements from IAT v1.7                                                                |\n| 3       | Focal persons         | Positions and alternates on both sides                                                                             |\n| 4       | Actions for the year  | From the IAT recommended actions and the CAPA register; outputs and dates                                          |\n| 5       | Information exchanged | What the CDRRMO supplies (hazard maps, scenarios, event data) and what the lead office supplies (evidence, status) |\n| 6       | Role in events        | PDRA participation; anticipatory actions; reporting to the EOC                                                     |\n| 7       | Review                | Annual interface review; self-scoring with validation by another office                                            |\n\n## Annex 8-D. Agenda of the Annual Partner Forum\n\n**Table 8.34**\n\n*Annual Partner Forum Agenda*\n\n| **No.** | **Item**                         | **Output**                                                                      |\n|---------|----------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Season outlook and hazard update | Shared understanding of the coming season (PAGASA products presented as issued) |\n| 2       | What we learned last season      | AAR findings involving partners; agreed improvements                            |\n| 3       | Partner register review          | Confirmed roles, contacts and commitments; lapsing agreements identified        |\n| 4       | Interfaces and lifelines         | Status of Part C actions and utility arrangements                               |\n| 5       | Inclusion and accountability     | Input from sectoral, faith-based and community groups                           |\n| 6       | Exercises for the year           | Partner participation in the exercise calendar (Chapter 9)                      |\n| 7       | Actions                          | Owners and dates entered in the CAPA register                                   |\n\n## Validation and Source Control Register\n\n**Table 8.35**\n\n*Validation and Source Control Register*\n\n| **Item**                              | **Source Used**                                                                                         | **Status**                                                     |\n|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|\n| IAT rows and scores                   | IAT v1.7 workbook in the repository (12 Nov 2026)                                                       | Pending validation, 1–4 December 2026                          |\n| Inter-LGU assistance records          | CDRRMC and SP resolutions in the City issuances register                      